Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Construction of site-specific weights", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534548666509458*^9, 3.534548675442284*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
The motion executed by our walker is an idealized discontinuous motion to \
which the concepts of kinematics do not pertain; it cannot in any standard \
sense be said to possess a \"velocity,\" and certainly not an \"acceleration.\
\" Its motion is therefore not in any standard sense \"dynamical,\" \
responsive to impressed \"forces.\" The familiar dynamical resources\
\[LongDash]potential, Hamiltonian, Lagrangian\[LongDash]are therefore not \
available to serve as devices from which to extract evaluations of the \
site-specific weight factors \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534565121509322*^9, 3.534565172859312*^9}, {
  3.534565382113072*^9, 3.534565436309576*^9}, {3.534565477939205*^9, 
  3.5345655833886633`*^9}, {3.534565617777637*^9, 3.5345657151300373`*^9}, {
  3.534609628341383*^9, 3.534609700689446*^9}, {3.5346097489932213`*^9, 
  3.534609750401309*^9}, {3.534609793182172*^9, 3.534609796027688*^9}, {
  3.5346098418987494`*^9, 3.5346098454112864`*^9}, {3.5346098914733963`*^9, 
  3.534609923591875*^9}, {3.534619067026355*^9, 3.5346190758700457`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["w", "1"], "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["w", "2"], "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["w", "3"], "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534609929205124*^9, 3.534609955729546*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534694290718196*^9, 3.5346942909621143`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["REMARK",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": In \"Letter to Patrick Tam 1\" (22 December 2011) I describe a random \
walk on\n2-dimensional ",
 StyleBox["phase",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " space in which the oscillator Hamiltonian ",
 StyleBox["is",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["used to control step-length, ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "and randomness enters only into the decision whether the next step will be \
a \[Delta]x-step or a\n\[Delta]p-step. The resulting walks look typically \
like these:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534690610849807*^9, 3.53469062056386*^9}, {
  3.53469338424907*^9, 3.5346935376521873`*^9}, {3.534693579752316*^9, 
  3.534693691165964*^9}, {3.534693737490408*^9, 3.5346937668779984`*^9}, {
  3.534694325882586*^9, 3.53469434508809*^9}}],

